# Findings Trivy reports and we accept. One reason per ID. Used by `trivy config`
# (scripts/trivy-config.sh, the lint job) and by the build job's image scan.
# A plain ignore file applies to every file, so each ID here is accepted repo-wide.

# Storage account of the Terraform state (infra/base/main.tf): no network rules, public endpoint.
# GitLab.com runners have no fixed IP and no path into the VNet. Shared keys, local users and
# anonymous access are off, so every request needs an Entra role.
AZU-0012

# NSG rule allow-node-https-out (infra/lab/nsg.tf): node egress to the Internet on 443.
# Outbound control is decided at the Azure step (Azure Firewall or ACNS), see docs/azure.md.
AZU-0051

# ConfigMap db-sql (chart, kind and Azure): "stores secrets" is a false positive. The match is
# `CREATE ROLE ... PASSWORD :'pw_<role>'` in db/sql/02-roles.sql, a psql variable; the passwords
# come from Secrets (kind) or Key Vault (Azure) and are passed to psql by init.sh.
KSV-0109
